(4019240, 569325, 48228, '<td valign="top">WOW this is lovely Sandy, and I see two of my favorite DPC friends sitting side by side..... <br/> <br/>Way to go Sandy and Brian.....</td>', 'WOW this is lovely Sandy, and I see two of my favorite DPC friends sitting side by side.....  Way to go Sandy and Brian.....', '2007-08-22 01:21:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(4019241, 571341, 56880, '<td valign="top">The low dust cloud and slight ridge between the town and the power grid really add to their sense of motion.  I really liked this shot.  You might have cropped the power lines on the right, and brought the left side in a bit to keep the rest balanced.</td>', 'The low dust cloud and slight ridge between the town and the power grid really add to their sense of motion.  I really liked this shot.  You might have cropped the power lines on the right, and brought the left side in a bit to keep the rest balanced.', '2007-08-22 01:21:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(4019246, 569915, 56880, '<td valign="top">Great job on getting the reflections right, and catching the late light in the sky and on the lake.</td>', 'Great job on getting the reflections right, and catching the late light in the sky and on the lake.', '2007-08-22 01:23:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(4019248, 571479, 22301, '<td valign="top">Excellent, I like this one much more than your FS entry. Into favs.</td>', 'Excellent, I like this one much more than your FS entry. Into favs.', '2007-08-22 01:23:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(4019249, 571298, 48228, '<td valign="top">WOW this is such a lovely soothing very peaceful early morning image here, from you Brian. <br/> <br/>I see two of my favorite DPC friends sitting side by side..... <br/> <br/>Way to go Sandy and Brian.....</td>', 'WOW this is such a lovely soothing very peaceful early morning image here, from you Brian.  I see two of my favorite DPC friends sitting side by side.....  Way to go Sandy and Brian.....', '2007-08-22 01:23:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(4019256, 570173, 56880, '<td valign="top">A tighter crop or wider DOF would have really helped this shot.  The outhouse on the far right is "too close," and nobody wants to be "too close" to one of those.  You can almost smell it through the screen.  On the other side, the tree trunk just poking in like that is distracting.  Since it does give a shadow on the back side, you might have included more of the trunk in the shot.</td>', 'A tighter crop or wider DOF would have really helped this shot.  The outhouse on the far right is "too close," and nobody wants to be "too close" to one of those.  You can almost smell it through the screen.  On the other side, the tree trunk just poking in like that is distracting.  Since it does give a shadow on the back side, you might have included more of the trunk in the shot.', '2007-08-22 01:25:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(4019257, 571479, 57775, '<td valign="top">Wow, de ja vu!  Congrats again William - It''s an amazing shot that can win 2 ribbons in a row!</td>', 'Wow, de ja vu!  Congrats again William - It''s an amazing shot that can win 2 ribbons in a row!', '2007-08-22 01:26:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(4019259, 570781, 78021, '<td valign="top">WOOHOO!  Went from my personal worst to my personal best back-to-back! :-)  I think some of the comments on this entry is going to help me on future entries too.  Thank you all! :-)</td>', 'WOOHOO!  Went from my personal worst to my personal best back-to-back! :-)  I think some of the comments on this entry is going to help me on future entries too.  Thank you all! :-)', '2007-08-22 01:26:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(4019263, 571298, 56880, '<td valign="top">The brick path leads me into the picture, but then I get stuck about 1/3 the way in.  The contrast between the tree in the foreground and the distant bridge and stoplights was nicely captured.</td>', 'The brick path leads me into the picture, but then I get stuck about 1/3 the way in.  The contrast between the tree in the foreground and the distant bridge and stoplights was nicely captured.', '2007-08-22 01:27:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(4019265, 571427, 40718, '<td valign="top">Ah, brutal!  The green ribbon on a 7.22.  Ya, that stings a bit.  But you have an awesome shot here.</td>', 'Ah, brutal!  The green ribbon on a 7.22.  Ya, that stings a bit.  But you have an awesome shot here.', '2007-08-22 01:27:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(4019266, 570690, 60862, '<td valign="top">Congrats, Rob!  Wow - top 10 and your personal best.  It''s a beautiful shot.</td>', 'Congrats, Rob!  Wow - top 10 and your personal best.  It''s a beautiful shot.', '2007-08-22 01:27:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(4019267, 571486, 57775, '<td valign="top">I''m glad this ribboned - this was one of my favorites in the challenge.  Beautiful work.</td>', 'I''m glad this ribboned - this was one of my favorites in the challenge.  Beautiful work.', '2007-08-22 01:28:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(4019268, 571479, 59267, '<td valign="top">Thank you so much everybody, especially to all the commenters and voters. :-)<br/> <br/>I think this is my once in life picture. The clouds, the lights, the reflections and the romantic couple have to all present at the right location. I wonder if I can find another lucky chance to shoot a photo like this again.<br/>Thanks you all for the comments.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-08-22 01:30:40.</i></td>', 'Thank you so much everybody, especially to all the commenters and voters. :-) I think this is my once in life picture. The clouds, the lights, the reflections and the romantic couple have to all present at the right location. I wonder if I can find another lucky chance to shoot a photo like this again.Thanks you all for the comments.', '2007-08-22 01:28:27.000000', '2007-08-22 02:30:40.000000', 0),
(4019272, 569843, 5705, '<td valign="top">Rocking the point and shoot, this is so glad to see-- congrats<br/></td>', 'Rocking the point and shoot, this is so glad to see-- congrats', '2007-08-22 01:30:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(4019273, 568953, 56880, '<td valign="top">This shot doesn''t give me the sense of "landscape," either on the normal or macro level.  It''s a good quick capture, given your conditions.  There seems to be more of the scene to the right, and including it might have given more of a story to the flipped minivan.  The people are backlit, so you kinda lose on getting good detail in their faces, and your camera bumped up the exposure to get the scene but by doing so it let the sky get overexposed.</td>', 'This shot doesn''t give me the sense of "landscape," either on the normal or macro level.  It''s a good quick capture, given your conditions.  There seems to be more of the scene to the right, and including it might have given more of a story to the flipped minivan.  The people are backlit, so you kinda lose on getting good detail in their faces, and your camera bumped up the exposure to get the scene but by doing so it let the sky get overexposed.', '2007-08-22 01:31:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(4019276, 570488, 75386, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Melethia:</b></div><hr/><i>   Second, how do you edit comments DURING the challenge?? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Its a 7+ scorers privilege!<br/> <br/>Great photo, the buildings look like they are paper cut outs, really cool</td>', 'Originally posted by Melethia:   Second, how do you edit comments DURING the challenge??   Its a 7+ scorers privilege! Great photo, the buildings look like they are paper cut outs, really cool', '2007-08-22 01:31:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(4019281, 570690, 19978, '<td valign="top">Nice job Rob. I immediately pegged this as either you or Maya. Congrats on a great finish!</td>', 'Nice job Rob. I immediately pegged this as either you or Maya. Congrats on a great finish!', '2007-08-22 01:33:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(4019287, 571486, 5112, '<td valign="top">Hi there, many congratulations!  I''m very glad this ribboned!</td>', 'Hi there, many congratulations!  I''m very glad this ribboned!', '2007-08-22 01:35:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(4019291, 569843, 5112, '<td valign="top">David, way to go!!!!  Many congratulations!</td>', 'David, way to go!!!!  Many congratulations!', '2007-08-22 01:36:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(4019295, 570781, 78021, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Citadel:</b></div><hr/><i> This could use a quick touchup of levels and/or curves. Nothing''s really black and nothing is white. I would include more of the building on the righr as well. Otherwise I like the composition and the colors are quite nice. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks for the "Curves" recomendation.  I never realy knew what "Curves" where, but after looking up a few "Curves" tutorials online...I can''t beleive I''d not used them before.  The ability to adjust low, med, and high tones independantly is amaizing.  I re-edited this scene with curves...it was sooo much better!  This is something I will certanly use in the future (already have on this weeks entry).<br/> <br/>I agree I the composition would have been better if the building on the right was not cut-off...unfortunatly that is how it was captured.  Maybe I should have cropped at the edge of the first building on the right...but I would have lost the panoramic effect. But it would have corrected the smallness pointed out by Smardaz...it looked great at 100%, but I agree the details are small at 640 wide.<br/> <br/>Thanks everybody for your comments.  They where very helpful this time. :-)</td>', 'Originally posted by Citadel: This could use a quick touchup of levels and/or curves. Nothing''s really black and nothing is white. I would include more of the building on the righr as well. Otherwise I like the composition and the colors are quite nice.   Thanks for the "Curves" recomendation.  I never realy knew what "Curves" where, but after looking up a few "Curves" tutorials online...I can''t beleive I''d not used them before.  The ability to adjust low, med, and high tones independantly is amaizing.  I re-edited this scene with curves...it was sooo much better!  This is something I will certanly use in the future (already have on this weeks entry). I agree I the composition would have been better if the building on the right was not cut-off...unfortunatly that is how it was captured.  Maybe I should have cropped at the edge of the first building on the right...but I would have lost the panoramic effect. But it would have corrected the smallness pointed out by Smardaz...it looked great at 100%, but I agree the details are small at 640 wide. Thanks everybody for your comments.  They where very helpful this time. :-)', '2007-08-22 01:37:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(4019300, 571479, 52549, '<td valign="top">Another beauty, William. That is, indeed, a magical spot. Congratulations on winning the blue. Great work.</td>', 'Another beauty, William. That is, indeed, a magical spot. Congratulations on winning the blue. Great work.', '2007-08-22 01:37:37.000000', NULL, 0),
