(4021239, 571479, 59267, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by sh0rty:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by sh0rty:</b></div><hr/><i> ...I think this one turned out nicer than the one you submitted for the other challange...so...I''ll keep my vote where it is. (maybe a first place for this one...if people do not change their minds after seeing it in the top three from the other challange?) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I guess not too many came back to mark it down for duplication. An awsome picture...the 2 ribbons prove it! Congrats! :-) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Actually my avg score stayed above 8.1 before Sunday night. The score dropped sharply after the Free Study XVII announcement. Almost all the lowest votes came on Monday; not due to duplication, just because attackers found the target. If you observe the "voting breakdown", I got two 1s and three 3s for this photo but all clear for the other one.<br/> <br/>FYI...<br/>Urban Landscapes II<br/> <br/>Votes: 173  <br/>Views: 318  <br/>Avg Vote: 8.1040  <br/>Comments: 32  <br/>Favorites: 5  <br/>Wish Lists: 1  <br/>Updated: 08/20/07 03:10 am <br/>Status: Your submission has been validated, thank you. <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by sh0rty: Originally posted by sh0rty: ...I think this one turned out nicer than the one you submitted for the other challange...so...I''ll keep my vote where it is. (maybe a first place for this one...if people do not change their minds after seeing it in the top three from the other challange?)   I guess not too many came back to mark it down for duplication. An awsome picture...the 2 ribbons prove it! Congrats! :-)   Actually my avg score stayed above 8.1 before Sunday night. The score dropped sharply after the Free Study XVII announcement. Almost all the lowest votes came on Monday; not due to duplication, just because attackers found the target. If you observe the "voting breakdown", I got two 1s and three 3s for this photo but all clear for the other one. FYI...Urban Landscapes II Votes: 173  Views: 318  Avg Vote: 8.1040  Comments: 32  Favorites: 5  Wish Lists: 1  Updated: 08/20/07 03:10 am Status: Your submission has been validated, thank you. ', '2007-08-22 14:21:11.000000', NULL, 0),
