(4022919, 571819, 71105, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by potoche:</b></div><hr/><i> Haha!<br/>Ok my comment saying that the saturations have exploded on this image made me elligible for a wonderful PM from the author :) :) :)<br/> <br/>so let me explain myself<br/>I mean that you''ve pushed too far your lovely sat slider. If you look at the bakground buildings, the color channel is way too strong for a luminosity channel that you''ve left fairly high.<br/> <br/>Atmosphere and pollution make the far objects look uncontrasted and desaturated. If you try to reverse that, you will end up with a false-looking pic<br/> <br/>Let me apologise myself if i wasn''t clear in my first message. </i></td></tr></table>\<br/> <br/>Clear enough, but I still like my picture.  Thanks for the first rate critique.</td>', 'Originally posted by potoche: Haha!Ok my comment saying that the saturations have exploded on this image made me elligible for a wonderful PM from the author :) :) :) so let me explain myselfI mean that you''ve pushed too far your lovely sat slider. If you look at the bakground buildings, the color channel is way too strong for a luminosity channel that you''ve left fairly high. Atmosphere and pollution make the far objects look uncontrasted and desaturated. If you try to reverse that, you will end up with a false-looking pic Let me apologise myself if i wasn''t clear in my first message. \ Clear enough, but I still like my picture.  Thanks for the first rate critique.', '2007-08-23 00:29:50.000000', NULL, 0),
