(4024378, 571704, 3032, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by junior_z:</b></div><hr/><i> How do you get these Russian letters in this äàìíåä ÄèÏèÑè ñàéò? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>&amp;#1071; &amp;#1085;&amp;#1077; &amp;#1079;&amp;#1085;&amp;#1072;&amp;#1102; :)<br/> <br/>The strange stuff above means Ja ne znaju.<br/> <br/>It works in the photographers comments field, but not in the forum and comment sections. When I edit my post I do see the original cyrillic. For some reason the forum software does not take it over or the browsers cannot handle it in the forum fields.<br/> <br/>I use online translators and some text I type in a virtual Russian keyboard. A small bit of code that turns my English keyboard into a Russian one. :)<br/><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-08-23 15:19:21.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by junior_z: How do you get these Russian letters in this äàìíåä ÄèÏèÑè ñàéò?   &#1071; &#1085;&#1077; &#1079;&#1085;&#1072;&#1102; :) The strange stuff above means Ja ne znaju. It works in the photographers comments field, but not in the forum and comment sections. When I edit my post I do see the original cyrillic. For some reason the forum software does not take it over or the browsers cannot handle it in the forum fields. I use online translators and some text I type in a virtual Russian keyboard. A small bit of code that turns my English keyboard into a Russian one. :)', '2007-08-23 16:14:55.000000', '2007-08-23 16:19:21.000000', 0),
