(4033169, 571341, 67145, '<td valign="top">amazing place you''ve photographed here .. those structures look like weird aliens &amp; they fit in so well in this alien landscape and the buildings .. very much a day of the triffids feel to me .. and yes very different .. are those birds or something on all the wires ??.. and i mean ALL the wires .. probably not .. they''re probably transformers or something electrical .. :)</td>', 'amazing place you''ve photographed here .. those structures look like weird aliens & they fit in so well in this alien landscape and the buildings .. very much a day of the triffids feel to me .. and yes very different .. are those birds or something on all the wires ??.. and i mean ALL the wires .. probably not .. they''re probably transformers or something electrical .. :)', '2007-08-27 17:48:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(4035688, 570226, 16488, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>A simple action shot of two casual basketball players in an urban setting. For a landscape challenge this is an out of the box entry. I think I can see where you were going with the idea--including activity against a backdrop of buildings. But I have to agree with the voters that the landscape isn''t strong enough for the challenge. The subject here is really the players.<br/> <br/>This is a fair stop-action image that a little more air-time would have helped. The technical quality of the image is lacking, as many of your commentors noted. The focus is a bit soft, the sharpness, contrast and saturation are a bit ho-hum. I can appreciate that this is your first attempt at RAW and so, perhaps, you are still finding your way with the post processing.<br/> <br/>My main criticism is the composition. The background is very busy...there are two nets, signs to read, stray shadows and a bush intruding on the composition. There are also mergers that distract the eye--the pole behind the players and again the pole and the net. The fact that these mergers are similar and echo one another multiplies the effect. Someone at DPC once suggested that a good way to make an image was to find an interesting background and wait for something to happen in front of it. I think that sort of planning would have helped you pull off this subject a bit better.<br/> <br/>Overall this is a subject worth revisiting with a new perspective on what you''re trying to shoot.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! A simple action shot of two casual basketball players in an urban setting. For a landscape challenge this is an out of the box entry. I think I can see where you were going with the idea--including activity against a backdrop of buildings. But I have to agree with the voters that the landscape isn''t strong enough for the challenge. The subject here is really the players. This is a fair stop-action image that a little more air-time would have helped. The technical quality of the image is lacking, as many of your commentors noted. The focus is a bit soft, the sharpness, contrast and saturation are a bit ho-hum. I can appreciate that this is your first attempt at RAW and so, perhaps, you are still finding your way with the post processing. My main criticism is the composition. The background is very busy...there are two nets, signs to read, stray shadows and a bush intruding on the composition. There are also mergers that distract the eye--the pole behind the players and again the pole and the net. The fact that these mergers are similar and echo one another multiplies the effect. Someone at DPC once suggested that a good way to make an image was to find an interesting background and wait for something to happen in front of it. I think that sort of planning would have helped you pull off this subject a bit better. Overall this is a subject worth revisiting with a new perspective on what you''re trying to shoot.', '2007-08-28 15:43:48.000000', NULL, 0),
